C", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 751103, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary:\n\n**Root cause:** `src/money.py::round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` while its docstring, FIN-212, and `tests/test_money.py` all call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). `Decimal(\"2.665\")` was rounding to `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Created branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from `main`.\n2. Changed the import and `quantize(...)` call to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n3. Ran CI (`ci-0001`) \u2014 passed.\n4. The PR was initially rejected because `main` had moved ahead, so I merged `main` into the branch (`0a9452f727`), verified the fix was intact after the merge, and re-ran CI (`ci-0002`) \u2014 passed.\n5. Opened **PR #101** against `main` with `alex` requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR, since merging into `main` requires code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GS6KNTe1eCtMUoSsseUemB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CEtUvk6WUSN3yznxx5hrEv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll create a branch and commit the fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01436teKQeYBiK23dRJaf7fP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": n